## 8.4.5Unformatted text input

The following listing shows a function that has functionality equivalent to fgets . Again, such example code is not meant to replace the function but to illustrate properties of the functions in question: here, the error-handling strategy.

```c
char* fgets_manually(char s[restrict], int n,
                     FILE*restrict stream) {
  if (!stream) return nullptr;
  if (!n) return s;
  /* Reads at most n-1 characters */
  for (size_t i = 0; i < n-1; ++i) {
    int val = fgetc(stream);
    switch (val) {
      /* EOF signals end-of-file or error */
      case EOF: if (feof(stream)) {
        s[i] = 0;
        /* Has been a valid call */
        return s;
      } else {
        /* Error */
        return nullptr;
      }
      /* Stop at end-of-line. */
      case '\n': s[i] = val; s[i+1] = 0; return s;
      /* Otherwise just assign and continue. */
      default: s[i] = val;
    }
  }
  s[n-1] = 0;
  return s;
}
```

