Since stdout is line buffered, we only check for eofOut when we write the ’’ character. This happens inside the short function end_line : The function longjmp comes with a companion macro setjmp that is used to establish a jump target to which a call of longjmp may refer. The header <setjmp.h> provides the following prototypes:

```c
char const* end_line(char const s[static 1], jmp_buf jmpTarget) {
