The following snippet provides a basic example of how this is supposed to be used: Here, we have a global variable ( errlog ) that needs dynamic initialization (calls to time , srand , rand , snprintf , fopen , and setvbuf ) for its initialization. Any usage of that variable should be prefixed with a call to call_once that uses the same once_flag (here, errlog_flag ) and the same callback function (here, errlog_fopen ).

