## Example: Continue Statement with Nested Loops

In the example below, there are three **for** loops one inside the other. These loops are controlled by the variables **i**, **j**, and **k** respectively. The innermost loop skips the printf statement if **k** is equal to either **i** or **j**, and goes to its next value of **k**. The second **j** loop executes the **continue** when it equals **i**. As a result, all the unique combinations of three digits 1, 2 and 3 are displayed. Run the code and check its output −

```c
for(j \= 1; j <= 3; j++){
     if (i \== j)
        continue;

     for (k\=1; k <= 3; k++){
        if (k \== j || k \== i)
           continue;

        printf("%d %d %d \\n", i,j,k);

     }
  }
```

