## Syntax

The syntax of the "switch" statement is as follows: The switch statement evaluates the expression once and then matches its value to one of the constants specified in the cases. The expression is usually an integer or a character, although it can also be an enumeration or a single-value floating-point variable.

```c
switch (expression) {
  case value1:
    // code to execute if expression matches value1
    break;

  case value2:
    // code to execute if expression matches value2
    break;

  // more cases can be added

  default:
    // code to execute if none of the cases match
}
```

