## Basic MIME Type Mapping

Browsers use the \`Contentâ€Type\` header to know how to display the received data. You will need a simple function that takes a file extension and returns the corresponding MIME type string. If the requested path is just \`/\` (the root of the web server), you should implicitly serve \`index.html\`.

```c
const char* get_mime_type(const char* file_path) {
    const char* ext = strrchr(file_path, '.'); // Find last '.'
    if (!ext) return "application/octet-stream"; // Default for unknown
    ext++; // Move past the dot

    if (strcmp(ext, "html") == 0 || strcmp(ext, "htm") == 0) return "text/html";
    if (strcmp(ext, "css") == 0) return "text/css";
    if (strcmp(ext, "js") == 0) return "application/javascript";
    if (strcmp(ext, "jpg") == 0 || strcmp(ext, "jpeg") == 0) return "image/jpeg";
    if (strcmp(ext, "png") == 0) return "image/png";
    if (strcmp(ext, "gif") == 0) return "image/gif";
    if (strcmp(ext, "txt") == 0) return "text/plain";
    // Add more as needed

    return "application/octet-stream";
}
```

